# Purpose

Enable the **Forge lifecycle MCP portfolio** on a product project scaffolded from the bootstrap toolkit, without vendoring Forge server code into the product repository.

Validated integration patterns come from the Project-1 harness (`nicksinx` Forge repos + OKF operator layer). Full policy detail lives in the bootstrap repo lessons: `.okf/improvements/forge-lifecycle-bootstrap-lessons.md` (bootstrap kit) and per-server repos.

# Architecture

```text
Cursor Desktop ──► user MCP (~/.cursor/mcp.json) and/or project .cursor/mcp.json
Cursor Cloud Agents ──► custom HTTP MCP on cursor.com/agents
        │  (Cloud does not see ~/.cursor/mcp.json; Desktop MCP is not inherited)
        ▼
HTTPS  https://forge-collection-mcp-server-nicksinxs-projects.vercel.app/api/mcp
        │  forge-collection  (Vercel map / gateway — not a Forge reimplementation)
        ▼
Optional FORGE_RUNTIME_URL → Node host with sibling clones + built dist/
  scripts/*-mcp.sh (stdio) → ../ConceptForge, ../LaunchForge, …

Product project (this repo)
  .cursor/mcp-forge-lifecycle.json.example  → HTTP collection (committed)
  .cursor/mcp.json                          → gitignored copy of the HTTP example
  .cursor/mcp-forge-stdio-siblings.json.example → Node-host stdio launchers only
  scripts/*-mcp.sh     → resolve sibling paths, pin versions
  .okf/forge/*         → per-server workspaces (gitignored)
  .okf/                → curated memory (promotion target)
```

**Option C integration:** OKF is the substrate; Forge owns lifecycle computation and signed packets; promotion to OKF is one-way and review-gated. See `.okf/decisions/0002-okf-forge-integration.md`.

Forge is **not** a sixth OKF bootstrap service. Enable Forge **after** the five-service OKF setup (Cursor → Codex → Claude → Xcode → Perplexity).

A new Forge-enabled product gets OKF + MCP **wiring** only. It does **not** spawn sibling servers. Forge runs where siblings were cloned and built: Desktop next to the project, each Cloud Agent environment, or one shared always-on runtime that the Vercel collection can forward to.

| Need | What must be running |
|------|----------------------|
| Catalog / packet map only | Vercel `/api/mcp` |
| Cloud Agents emit/import | Vercel **and** a reachable Node runtime (`FORGE_RUNTIME_URL`) |
| Desktop only with local stdio Forge | Sibling clones + `mcp-forge-stdio-siblings.json.example` — neither Vercel nor Docker required |

Bearer token on the public collection URL is **on hold**. Do not add `MCP_BEARER_TOKEN` to product templates.

# Setup order

1. Complete OKF bootstrap validation: `scripts/okf-validate`, `scripts/validate_launch.sh`.
2. **Cursor Desktop:** confirm HTTP `forge-collection` in Settings → MCP (user) and/or project `.cursor/mcp.json` (launcher copies the committed example).
3. **Cursor Cloud Agents:** add a **custom HTTP MCP** with URL `https://forge-collection-mcp-server-nicksinxs-projects.vercel.app/api/mcp`. Do not assume Desktop MCP or `~/.cursor/mcp.json` is visible.
4. Clone Forge siblings when you need real stage tools (optional helper): `scripts/forge-clone-siblings.sh`.
5. Build each Forge repo on the **Node host** that will run them: `cd ../<Repo> && npm ci && npm run build`.
6. Stdio launchers are the Node-host path only: `cp .cursor/mcp-forge-stdio-siblings.json.example .cursor/mcp.json` **instead of** the HTTP example if this Cursor session should spawn local siblings. Prefer keeping HTTP collection as the default project `mcp.json`.
7. Reload Cursor MCP. For stdio, confirm launchers resolve sibling `dist/index.js` (LaunchForge uses `mcp-server/dist/index.js`).
8. Run server smokes in sibling repos before relying on cross-MCP handoffs.

# Launcher conventions

Stdio bash launchers are the **Node-host** path (Mac, Cloud Agent snapshot, or always-on runtime). Default Cursor wiring is HTTP `forge-collection`, not these stdio entries.

| Pattern | Rationale |
|---------|-----------|
| Bash launcher in `scripts/<server>-mcp.sh` | Avoids `${env:VAR}` limitations in `.cursor/mcp.json` |
| `*_ROOT` defaults to `../<Repo>` | Sibling layout keeps product repo clean |
| `*_WORKSPACE` under `.okf/forge/<stage>/` | Gitignored runtime state, not OKF concepts |
| Version pin via `*_MIN_VERSION` env | Fail fast when sibling checkout drifts |
| `assert-contracts-version.mjs` when present | Shared `@forge-lifecycle/contracts` alignment |

Override roots when siblings are not peers, e.g. `export LAUNCHFORGE_ROOT=/path/to/LaunchForge`.

# Promotion and dispatch

| Layer | Use when |
|-------|----------|
| Forge MCP | Planning lifecycle stages, signed handoffs, readiness gates |
| OKF promotion | Integrator-reviewed outcomes → `.okf/` concepts with lineage |
| OKF dispatch | Implementation delivery (`scripts/okf-dispatch` when installed) |
| ForgeRelay | Cross-tool agent handoff — parallel to OKF handoffs, not a replacement |

Packet routing: `.okf/references/forge-packet-type-registry.md`.

# Gitignore

Forge workspaces under `.okf/forge/` must stay gitignored. Never commit signing keys, approval receipts, or PII from Forge workspaces.

